    lines+=['','| ACT8 deterministic control | Accuracy (%) | CE |','|---|---:|---:|']
    for name,v in s['control_summary'].items():lines.append(f'| {name} | {100*v[0]:.4f} | {v[1]:.8f} |')
    lines+=['','All paired differences/95% descriptive intervals are in statistics.json, with parentR1 at identical weight trajectories/T and parentR3 at equal active-node updates. Parent5000 five-model/ten-seed bootstrap draws are reused on fixed consumed images; these are not new independent replications or generalization confirmation. No outcome-driven budget, range or quality-gate selection occurs. R3 differs in activation coding, activation sampling and sample rounds, so its contrast is a design comparison rather than an isolated causal variance ablation.','','Every gated/column counter, hidden code and final output is checked against the already public-replayed same-key parentR1 per-weight counts. This exact sufficient-statistic identity audit adds zero new raw-state samples. The full new direct observer nevertheless executes304,584,000,000 scheduled native updates; earlier bounded public-state/operator and GPU paired preflights are separately charged. All original parent results and executed-work totals stay unchanged.','','Weights retain nominal8-bit field commands. Input/hidden ranges are four F64 scalars per model, and activations have deterministic8-bit codes; biases remain FP32. Native counters are int32 and evidence counters uint32. The output-counter state is378 counters versus2368 per-weight counters; the first-layer bound255*64*1568=25,589,760 needs25 unsigned bits. Wider integer gates, control/DAC storage, activation/readout buffers and clocks are distinct unmeasured hardware costs. Sampler simulation uses floating probability arithmetic; final readout uses F64. No physical energy/latency/area or total-memory advantage follows.','','The ACT8 programmed-mean control is a nonlinear plug-in, not E[stochastic NN]. Low-bit controls use dequantized software arithmetic, not optimized integer kernels. Broader CNN/Transformer coverage and actual hardware measurements remain open; the long-horizon goal remains active.','','[Protocol](integer_activation_native/cohort/protocol.json) · [Native count/causal audit](integer_activation_native/cohort/evidence_audit.json) · [All statistics](integer_activation_native/cohort/statistics.json) · [Statistics audit](integer_activation_native/cohort/statistics_audit.json).']
    report=Path('results/thrml_spw/INTEGER_ACTIVATION_CLASSIFIER_REPORT.md');report.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');paths=[OUT/n for n in ['protocol.json','manifest.json','evidence_audit.json','statistics.json','statistics_audit.json','control_logits.npz','statistical_arrays.npz']]+[report];atomic_json(OUT/'completion.json',{'status':'full_native_integer_activation_classifier_audited_goal_active','recorded_utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'production_updates':304584000000,'new_raw_public_audit_updates':0,'native_cases':150,'artifact_sha256':{str(f):sha(f) for f in paths}});print('Full integer-activation classifier statistics independently audited/report complete',flush=True)
